---
// src/pages/outdoor/brands/napoleon.astro
// Napoleon grill brand page. Built to twin-eagles.astro / bull.astro pattern.
// Verified models only: Prestige series, Prestige PRO 500/665 (freestanding PRO500RSIBPSS-3 / PRO665RSIBPSS-3),
//   Built-in Prestige PRO (BIPRO500RBSS-3 / BIPRO665RBNSS-3), Rogue (425/525/625).
//   Features: JETFIRE ignition, infrared SIZZLE ZONE side burner, infrared rear burner, WAVE cooking grids.
//   Napoleon = Wolf Steel Ltd (Barrie, Ontario, Canada), mid-premium. Honest scope: closer to consumer than the ultra-premium built-ins.
// Em-dash budget in visible body: keep low. Voice: "our techs" / "we". $89 outdoor diagnostic.

import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE } from '../../../data/branches';

import { mergeCredentials } from '../../../data/credentials-schema';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../../lib/build-location-array';
const phone = MAIN_PHONE;
const phoneRaw = MAIN_PHONE.replace(/\D/g, '');
const phoneHref = `tel:+1${phoneRaw}`;
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/outdoor/brands/napoleon/";

const title = "Napoleon Grill Repair Los Angeles — Same Day";
const description = `Napoleon grill repair across SoCal. Prestige, Prestige PRO 500/665, Rogue. JETFIRE ignition, infrared side and rear burners. $89 diagnostic. ${phone}.`;

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What Napoleon grills do you repair in Los Angeles?",
    a: "The Napoleon gas grill lineup: the Prestige series, the Prestige PRO 500 and 665 (freestanding and built-in configurations), and the Rogue series. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair service the JETFIRE ignition system, the infrared SIZZLE ZONE side burner, the infrared rear burner for the rotisserie, the WAVE cooking grids, and the standard tube burners across all five SoCal counties. Both natural gas and liquid propane."
  },
  {
    q: "My Napoleon won't light with the JETFIRE ignition. What's wrong?",
    a: "Napoleon uses a JETFIRE electronic ignition that lights each burner individually. When one burner won't light, the usual cause is a worn or fouled ignition electrode on that burner, or a dead battery on the units that use one. When nothing lights at all, it is more often the battery or a wiring fault at the module. Our techs test the electrode, the battery, and the gas flow in sequence rather than guessing, and these are inexpensive parts."
  },
  {
    q: "The infrared side or rear burner on my Napoleon stopped working. Is that a normal burner?",
    a: "No. Napoleon's infrared SIZZLE ZONE side burner and the infrared rear burner (behind the rotisserie) run hotter and cycle harder than the standard tube burners, so they wear differently and fail earlier. When a Napoleon sear zone or rear burner quits while the main grill works, we diagnose the infrared element and the ignition feeding it separately. It is a different part and a different repair than a main tube burner."
  },
  {
    q: "Are Napoleon parts easy to get, and is repair worth it?",
    a: "Yes on both. Napoleon is a mid-premium brand with widely available parts, so electrodes, burners, igniters, and WAVE cooking grids are inexpensive and we often source them fast. A built-in Prestige PRO is a real investment worth repairing for almost any single-component failure. On an older freestanding Rogue, we give you the honest math: if a stacked repair on a low-cost cart approaches the price of a new unit, we tell you straight rather than talking you into it."
  },
  {
    q: "How long do Napoleon grills last in Los Angeles?",
    a: "With repair and maintenance, a built-in Prestige PRO gives 12 to 18 years, and the freestanding Prestige and Rogue carts run a bit less. Salt air is the limiter on the coast, in Malibu, Newport Beach, and Pacific Palisades the tube burners and electrodes corrode faster than they do inland. Replacing a corroded burner at the first sign keeps the manifold from taking damage downstream."
  },
  {
    q: "My Napoleon is built into an island. Does that change the repair?",
    a: "Access changes, the diagnosis does not. Our techs work the built-in Prestige PRO 500 and 665 from the front of a BBQ island, swapping burners, electrodes, and the infrared burners without pulling the whole grill out of the surround. On LP setups we confirm the regulator and gas line before re-firing each zone. $89 outdoor diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "What's your warranty on Napoleon repairs?",
    a: "Ninety days SDAR parts-and-labor warranty on the work we perform. Napoleon carries strong manufacturer coverage on many grill components, so if the failure looks warranty-eligible we tell you before any out-of-pocket work and help you process the claim. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified, and BBB Accredited Business."
  }
];

