<!-- 01 INTRO -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Napoleon service</p>
    <h2>Napoleon's infrared burners and JETFIRE ignition are what we see fail.</h2>

    <p><strong>When a Napoleon grill fails at an LA home, our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair trace it to a few patterns: a JETFIRE ignition electrode out on one burner, the infrared SIZZLE ZONE side burner or the infrared rear burner failing while the main grill still cooks, a salt-corroded tube burner on a coastal install, or a worn regulator dropping flame across the zones. These are the Prestige PRO built-ins in BBQ islands and the Prestige and Rogue carts on patios across the five counties, and coastal salt sets the corrosion clock. $89 outdoor diagnostic, waived with repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), BBB Accredited.</strong></p>

    <p class="intro-speakable">Napoleon is a Canadian manufacturer, Wolf Steel Ltd, based in Barrie, Ontario. In our SoCal territory Napoleon lands as a mid-premium grill: the built-in Prestige PRO 500 and 665 in outdoor kitchens, and the freestanding Prestige and Rogue carts on patios where the owner wanted infrared searing and a rotisserie without the ultra-premium price of a Lynx or Twin Eagles. That positioning shapes our advice. A built-in Prestige PRO is worth repairing for almost any single failure, while on an older low-cost Rogue cart we give you the honest repair-versus-replace math.</p>

    <p>Our techs service the Napoleon gas lineup: the Prestige series, the Prestige PRO 500 and 665 (freestanding RSIB models and built-in RB models), and the Rogue series. We handle JETFIRE ignition, the infrared SIZZLE ZONE side burner, the infrared rear rotisserie burner, WAVE cooking grids, standard tube burners, and regulators, in natural gas and liquid propane.</p>

    <p>BHGS #A49573. Same-day across LA, Orange County, Ventura. Common Napoleon electrodes and burners on the van.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 NAPOLEON SERIES -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">Series and architecture</p>
    <h2>Napoleon series and what fails on each.</h2>

    <p class="lead">Napoleon grills share a common feature set (JETFIRE ignition, infrared burner options, WAVE grids) across three tiers. We identify by the full model before ordering, because the built-in and freestanding versions of the same series can take different parts.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Prestige PRO 500 and 665 (flagship)</h3>
    <p>The top of Napoleon's grill line. The freestanding models carry RSIB in the name (PRO500RSIBPSS-3, PRO665RSIBPSS-3), and the built-in island versions carry RB (BIPRO500RBSS-3, BIPRO665RBNSS-3). The 500 is a 6-burner and the 665 an 8-burner. Both include the infrared SIZZLE ZONE side burner and an infrared rear burner for the rotisserie. Common failures concentrate at the two infrared burners and the JETFIRE electrodes.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Prestige series (classic)</h3>
    <p>The standard Prestige line below the PRO. Same JETFIRE ignition and WAVE cooking grids, often with the infrared rear burner. Failures we see are ignition electrodes, tube burner corrosion on coastal installs, and rear-burner wear on grills used heavily for rotisserie cooking.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Rogue series</h3>
    <p>Napoleon's value cart line (Rogue 425, 525, 625). Simpler feature set, JETFIRE ignition, some with an infrared side or rear burner. These are freestanding carts, closer to consumer-grade than the built-ins, so the honest repair-versus-replace conversation matters more here on older units.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">JETFIRE ignition</h3>
    <p>Napoleon's JETFIRE system lights each burner individually. A single dead burner is usually its electrode; a whole-grill no-light is more often the battery or a wiring fault. Inexpensive parts, quick swap, high misdiagnosis rate when a shop replaces burners instead of the electrode.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Infrared burners, WAVE grids, rotisserie</h3>
    <p><strong>SIZZLE ZONE infrared side burner:</strong> high-heat searing station, runs hotter than the main burners and fails earlier. <strong>Infrared rear burner:</strong> behind the rotisserie, similar high-cycle wear. <strong>WAVE cooking grids:</strong> stainless or cast iron, corrode on coastal installs, replaced as a set. <strong>Rotisserie motor:</strong> standard replacement at end of life.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 TYPICAL SCENARIOS -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Common scenarios</p>
    <h2>Top Napoleon repairs in our 5-county territory.</h2>

    <p>Ranked by how often our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair see them, most common first.</p>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>JETFIRE electrode failure.</strong> Single burner won't light, others working. Test and replace the electrode for that zone.</li>
      <li><strong>Infrared burner failure (SIZZLE ZONE or rear).</strong> Sear zone or rear burner dead, main grill fine. Diagnose the infrared element and its ignition, then replace.</li>
      <li><strong>Whole-grill no-light.</strong> Dead battery or wiring fault at the JETFIRE module. Inexpensive fix.</li>
      <li><strong>Coastal tube burner corrosion.</strong> Salt-driven pinhole on Malibu and Newport Beach installs. Per-zone replacement before manifold damage.</li>
      <li><strong>Regulator drop.</strong> Low flame across all zones on LP setups. Regulator check and replacement.</li>
      <li><strong>WAVE cooking grid corrosion.</strong> Grids rust through on coastal grills. Replacement set.</li>
      <li><strong>Rotisserie motor.</strong> Seizure at end of life on rotisserie-equipped grills. Replacement.</li>
      <li><strong>Valve or knob issue.</strong> Sticking valve after seasonal inactivity. Clean, lubricate, occasionally replace.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 REAL REPAIR STORIES -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">Real repairs</p>
    <h2>Composite stories from the route.</h2>

    <p class="lead">Four Napoleon jobs typical of the past 90 days. Models, symptoms, diagnosis, time, total. Names omitted; the scenarios are what we see weekly.</p>

    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Irvine, Napoleon BIPRO665RB built-in (2019 install)</h3>
        <p>Infrared SIZZLE ZONE side burner would not light, main grill fine. Diagnosis: infrared element failed plus a fouled orifice. Replaced the side burner and cleared the orifice, tested the sear ignition. Total: $89 plus $200 part plus 1 hour = $349.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Beverly Hills, Napoleon PRO500RSIB (2020 install)</h3>
        <p>One main burner would not light on the JETFIRE ignition, others fine. Diagnosis: worn ignition electrode on that zone; battery and other electrodes tested clean. Replaced the electrode, verified spark and light on all burners. Total: $89 plus $70 part plus 40 minutes = $214.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Newport Beach, Napoleon Prestige (2017 install)</h3>
        <p>Uneven flame and a visible pinhole in one tube burner. Coastal install, salt corrosion at 8 years. Replaced the corroded burner before the manifold was affected and inspected the adjacent zones. Total: $89 plus $150 part plus 1 hour = $299.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Pasadena, Napoleon Rogue 625 cart (2016 install)</h3>
        <p>Whole grill would not light and the rear burner was dead at 9 years. Diagnosis: dead ignition battery plus a failed infrared rear burner. Replaced the battery and the rear burner, and gave the owner the honest math since the cart was aging. Total: $89 plus $180 parts plus 1 hour = $349.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 HONEST SCOPE -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Scope</p>
    <h2>What we do for Napoleon, and what we don't.</h2>

    <p><strong>We service:</strong></p>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>Prestige PRO 500 and 665 (freestanding RSIB and built-in RB)</li>
      <li>Prestige series grills</li>
      <li>Rogue series carts (425, 525, 625)</li>
      <li>JETFIRE ignition electrodes, batteries, and modules</li>
      <li>Infrared SIZZLE ZONE side burners and infrared rear burners</li>
      <li>Standard tube burners, WAVE cooking grids, regulators, rotisserie motors</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>We don't do:</strong> new grill installation (a gas-line trade); custom island or cabinetry modification (a fabrication trade); Napoleon home-heating products such as fireplaces and furnaces (a different service track). On an older low-cost Rogue cart, if a stacked repair approaches the price of a new unit, we will tell you straight.</p>

    <p>If your Napoleon is under manufacturer warranty, we can assess the failure and tell you whether it is warranty-eligible before any out-of-pocket work.</p>
  </div>
</section>

