<!-- 07 WHY US -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">Why us for Napoleon</p>
    <h2>What separates our Napoleon service from general grill repair.</h2>

    <ul class="reasons-list">
      <li><strong>Infrared burner fluency.</strong> The SIZZLE ZONE side burner and the infrared rear burner fail differently than the main tube burners. We diagnose the element and its ignition separately rather than swapping a whole burner on a guess.</li>
      <li><strong>JETFIRE ignition awareness.</strong> A single dead burner is usually the electrode, and a whole-grill no-light is usually the battery. We check the cheap cause first.</li>
      <li><strong>Built-in vs cart honesty.</strong> A Prestige PRO built-in is worth repairing for almost any failure; on an aging Rogue cart we give you the real repair-versus-replace number.</li>
      <li><strong>Coastal corrosion awareness.</strong> Malibu, Newport Beach, Pacific Palisades. Salt-driven burner and electrode failure is common, and we carry the parts on those routes.</li>
      <li><strong>Widely available parts.</strong> Napoleon electrodes, burners, and WAVE grids are inexpensive and fast to source, so most repairs finish quickly.</li>
      <li><strong>BHGS #A49573 plus EPA 608 Universal.</strong> Verifiable with the state and the bureau.</li>
      <li><strong>Same-day across LA, Orange County, Ventura. Next-day for Rancho Cucamonga and Temecula.</strong></li>
